- [ ] Inspect the final diff for `ds.root()`, custom pointer hosts, test-owned
      native focus shims, direct pointer-global writes, direct production
      `onInput()` calls, and direct production refresh/update shortcuts.
- [ ] Inspect the final diff for attempts to treat `plotinfo.hauling` or its
      procedural rows as widget paths.
- [ ] Inspect the final diff for accidental test-runner, dependency-bootstrap,
      or package-provisioning changes.
- [ ] Confirm `Run-AutomationTests.ps1` remains a direct pass-through to
      `dwarfspec run`.
- [ ] Report syntax, unit, mounted-component, registered-overlay, native-UI,
      and cleanup evidence separately.

## Completion gate

- [ ] Native interaction tests use borrowed native-screen attachments;
      addressable controls use selected `ds.get(...)` subjects, while
      procedural Hauling rows use production-derived screen-cell input and
      captured rendering/state evidence.
- [ ] Registered overlays remain owned by the DFHack registry throughout
      interaction tests.
- [ ] No native test depends on a custom host screen, pointer target, focus
      shim, or direct interaction lifecycle call.
- [ ] Deterministic component contracts are clearly separated from native
      production evidence.
- [ ] Syntax, unit, live component, cleanup, and final-diff evidence pass.
